Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `xs` was consumed by `xs.move()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/move_mark_binding.jet:6:5
    |
  6 |     xs.push(4)
    |     ^^
  --> tests/ui/move_mark_binding.jet:5:11
    |
  5 |     ys := xs.move()
    |           ^^^^^^^ `xs` moved to `xs.move()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `xs` after the move, or give `xs.move()` a copy with `xs.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
